R744 transcritical CO2 chiller — vineyard wine storage design data
===================================================================

Evaporating temperature (Tev):       {{tev_display}}
Useful superheat:                      {{useful_sh_k}} K
Suction superheat:                    {{suction_sh_k}} K
Gas-cooler exit temperature:         {{t_gc_exit_display}}
High-side pressure (gas cooler):     {{p_gc_display}}
Refrigerant:                         R744 (CO2)
Compression efficiency (η_comp):     {{eta_comp}}
Volumetric efficiency (η_vol):       {{eta_vol}}
Design cooling load (Q_design):      {{q_design_display}}

External boundaries (Carnot reference):
  Cellar air (T_L):                  {{t_cellar_display}}
  Outdoor ambient (T_H):             {{t_ambient_display}}

Notes:
  - Useful / suction superheat {{suction_sh_k}} K means the compressor inlet is
    {{suction_sh_k}} K above saturation at evaporator pressure
    (compressor inlet temperature = {{compressor_inlet_display}}).
  - When useful SH = suction SH, evaporator outlet and compressor inlet coincide.
  - Heat rejection is via a gas cooler at controlled high-side pressure
    {{p_gc_display}} — not a subcritical condenser.
  - Obtain R744 thermodynamic properties from any source you choose
    (tables, CoolProp/REFPROP, online tools, etc.) and document the source.
  - Deliverable must include cooling EER = q_evap / w_comp (W/W),
    Carnot comparison using T_L / T_H, mass flow ṁ = Q_design / q_evap,
    and displacement V̇_disp = ṁ · v1 / η_vol.
